      "text": "Since you get seasick, I'd stick with shorter trips closer to shore. The Full Day on the **San Diego** out of Seaforth is your best bet — it's the shortest option actually landing yellowfin lately.\n\n- **San Diego** (Full Day, $200–$250): Last 10 trips averaged **2.78 yellowfin per angler** — strongest tuna numbers of any short trip in the data. Win Rate **36%** (best of any boat here). Win Rate = % of same-day, same-length matchups where the boat had the best catch per angler.\n- **Malihini** (3/4 Day, $165): Shorter day on the water, averaging **1.66 yellowfin per angler** last 10 trips. Cheapest option and a Definite Go on Fri 11/27.\n- If you can handle one night but want to stay close-ish, the **Producer** Overnight ($360) has been landing **3.81 yellowfin per angler** last 10 trips — but it's a longer ride, so only if your stomach cooperates.\n\n<trip-card>{\"tripId\": \"1083153\", \"why\": [\"Shortest trip with real yellowfin numbers: 2.78 per angler last 10 trips\", \"Best Win Rate in the data at 36%\", \"19 of 36 spots open as of last update\"]}</trip-card>\n\n<trip-card>{\"tripId\": \"hm-6bdbce-11270730\", \"why\": [\"Shortest trip length (3/4 Day) — easiest on the stomach\", \"Last 10 trips: 1.66 yellowfin per angler\", \"Definite Go status, $165 as of last update\"]}</trip-card>\n\n<trip-card>{\"tripId\": \"hm-8b4572-11272000\", \"why\": [\"Last 10 trips: 3.81 yellowfin per angler — top tuna numbers in the short-trip range\", \"Definite Go, 14 of 29 spots open as of last update\"]}</trip-card>\n\nConfirm price and availability on the landing's site, and ask the crew or a pharmacist about seasickness remedies before you go.\n\n<followups>[\"Compare the San Diego vs Malihini\", \"What times do these return?\", \"Any cheaper Full Day options?\"]</followups>",
